---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial Independence & Affiliate Disclosure"
  seoTitle="Editorial Independence & Affiliate Disclosure"
  description="How Australian Home Collective uses affiliate links, protects editorial independence and reviews products before promotional placement."
>
  <header class="page-intro">
    <div class="narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Commercial relationships</p>
      <h1>Editorial Independence & Affiliate Disclosure</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Some links on Australian Home Collective are affiliate links. They help support the
        publication without changing what we research, conclude or recommend.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>
  <section class="content narrow">
    <h2>How affiliate links work</h2>
    <p>
      If you make a qualifying purchase through an affiliate link, Australian Home Collective may
      earn a commission at no extra cost to you. You are free to visit a retailer directly or buy
      elsewhere; using our links is never required.
    </p>
    <p>
      Affiliate revenue helps keep our guides free and the site clean, easy to use and free from
      intrusive display advertising. We may work with additional affiliate networks, retailers or
      other commercial partners over time, but the same editorial rules apply to every relationship.
    </p>

    <h2>Editorial independence comes first</h2>
    <p>
      Commercial relationships do not determine the topics we cover, the products we consider or
      the conclusions we reach. Products are not selected merely because they are popular,
      expensive, highly rated or pay a higher commission. Reader usefulness and suitability come
      before commercial value.
    </p>
    <p>
      A product can receive promotional affiliate placement only after it meets our documented
      {" "}<a href="/how-we-select-products/">AHC Product Research</a> standard and is separately
      approved for affiliate use. The surrounding guide must remain useful if a reader does not
      use the link.
    </p>

    <h2>Research, not implied testing</h2>
    <p>
      Unless a guide explicitly states what Australian Home Collective tested and how, we have not
      personally tested the product. Our assessments are based on research, including relevant
      manufacturer and warranty documents, independent expert or technical reviews, recurring
      owner-feedback themes, Australian availability and support, and regulator or recall checks
      where relevant.
    </p>
    <p>
      We publish material drawbacks, who an option may suit, who it may not suit, the evidence
      confidence and the date of the research review. A link is not a guarantee that a product will
      suit every household.
    </p>

    <h2>Ongoing review</h2>
    <p>
      Approved products are re-reviewed at least every 180 days and sooner when material new
      evidence emerges. A product may be downgraded, paused or removed if its specifications,
      availability, support, safety position or reliability evidence changes.
    </p>

    <h2>Reader choice</h2>
    <p>
      You are never required to use our links. Before buying, check the retailer's current
      product information, price, delivery details, returns policy and suitability for your
      household.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
